Kokoro is an open-weight text-to-speech model with 82 million
parameters that produces 24 kHz speech of a quality comparable to much
larger models.  This is its PyTorch inference library: KPipeline turns
text into phonemes with misaki and synthesizes them with a chosen
voice (American and British English; other languages need extra
misaki dependencies).

The model weights and voices are downloaded from Hugging Face
(hexgrad/Kokoro-82M) on first use.
